Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.74,0:03:22.02,Episode Title,,0,0,0,,{\fade(255,0,255,0,1000,3500,4250)\pos(640,465.962)}Episode 65\N\N\N\N\NCrossing the Lu River
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.10,0:03:50.18,Thinking,,0,0,0,,In the third year of the Jianxing Period (225 CE),
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.18,0:03:54.74,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Yong Kai, the administrator of Jianning Commandery of Shu-Han, allied with Meng Huo, King of the South,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.74,0:03:57.38,Thinking,,0,0,0,,and raised an army of 100,000 soldiers against Shu-Han.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.58,0:04:01.82,Thinking,,0,0,0,,The administrators of Yuejun and Zhangke Commanderies surrendered,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.82,0:04:05.82,Thinking,,0,0,0,,while leaving Yongchang Commandery besieged. The situation was critical.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.26,0:04:14.74,Thinking,,0,0,0,,When the news reached to the capital of Chengdu,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.54,0:04:14.74,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(999.062,446.943)}Chengdu
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.74,0:04:19.38,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang made the decision to lead the army personally to pacify the South.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.90,0:04:50.62,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(906.055,507.999)}	Zhūgě Liàng\NStyled: Kǒngmíng
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.82,0:04:58.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, bite!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.26,0:05:02.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Bite it! Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.06,0:05:04.98,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Do it! Bite!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.22,0:05:10.50,Default,,0,0,0,,-Go, bite it! \N-Oh look, Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.10,0:05:15.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.18,0:05:13.94,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(964.227,512.151)}Liú Shàn\NStyled: Gōngsì
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.66,0:05:16.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.58,0:05:20.50,Default,,0,0,0,,The Southern Tribes are revolting, Yongchang's situation is critical.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.82,0:05:23.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Bite!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.94,0:05:25.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.50,0:05:28.66,Default,,0,0,0,,King Meng Huo of the South is invading.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.86,0:05:31.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty ought to attend court.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.94,0:05:35.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Attending court...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.98,0:05:54.50,Default,,0,0,0,,The insurrection in the far south is a national crisis.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.50,0:05:58.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Your minister shall lead the army personally on an expedition.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.74,0:05:59.86,Default,,0,0,0,,No, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.90,0:06:02.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Father-Minister shouldn't leave Us!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.78,0:06:06.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Father-Minister, see...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.62,0:06:12.62,Default,,0,0,0,,With Sun Quan in the east and Cao Pi in the north, if Father-Minister leaves Us...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.62,0:06:16.70,Default,,0,0,0,,If Wu or Wei were to invade, what then?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.42,0:06:21.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}Our nation has restored relations \Nwith Eastern Wu; they would bear no hostility.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.58,0:06:24.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}Should they bear hostility,\NLi Yan guards the city of Baidi.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.98,0:06:27.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585\pos(640,679.245)}This man can resist Lu Xun.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.90,0:06:33.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}Cao Pi has recently suffered a defeat, so his spirit is too broken for a long campaign.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.02,0:06:37.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}Moreover, Ma Chao guards all strategic passes in Hanzhong.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.34,0:06:38.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585\pos(640,679.245)}There is no need for worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.94,0:06:43.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}Your minister has left Guan Xing and Zhang Bao \Nwith two detachments to guard you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.46,0:06:47.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585\pos(640,679.245)}Your Majesty will be safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.66,0:06:51.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}Your minister will pacify the South, then conquer the North.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.50,0:06:54.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}To retake the Central Plains, \Nand restore the Han Dynasty.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.58,0:06:58.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}To repay the late emperor's honor of the three visits and his entrustment of his heir.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.94,0:07:10.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Good. We are still young and ignorant, so you may act as you see fit.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.34,0:07:12.30,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(338.549,517.585)}Wáng Lián\NStyled: Wényí
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.58,0:07:14.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, you should not allow this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.94,0:07:20.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}Chancellor, the South is but a barren wilderness, home of pestilence.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.42,0:07:24.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}Chancellor holds responsibilities too great to allow personal expeditions.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.90,0:07:28.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}Assigning a single capable general is sufficient for the task.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.14,0:07:32.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}The southern frontier is far from the heart of the nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.18,0:07:34.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}{\pos(640,661.585)}Most people there do not know of our customs.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.62,0:07:40.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}To pacify them will be arduous. I must go there personally.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.42,0:07:45.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}The complexity of methods required cannot easily be entrusted to anyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.06,0:07:50.78,Default,,0,0,0,,With such dangerous roads ahead in scorching and deceitful lands,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.10,0:07:54.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, it truly is not proper for you to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.38,0:07:58.86,Default,,0,0,0,,If the South remains unstable, \Nthe North cannot be taken.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.54,0:08:04.94,Default,,0,0,0,,My march through hostile lands is not done in arrogance.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.34,0:08:10.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I only wish to fulfill the trust placed on me by the late emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.26,0:08:35.26,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(905.277,482.264)}Zhào Yún\NStyled: Zǐlóng
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.58,0:08:39.42,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(319.792,484.981)}Wèi Yán\NStyled: Wéncháng
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.42,0:08:43.26,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(338.549,459.17)}Wáng Píng \NStyled: Zijūn
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.78,0:08:57.10,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(749.113,394)}Yōng
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.34,0:09:07.38,Thinking,,0,0,0,,After Zhuge Liang arrived at Yunnan,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.58,0:09:13.30,Thinking,,0,0,0,,he eliminated the rebel leaders Yong Kai and Zhu Bao \Nby sowing dissension between them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.46,0:09:18.78,Thinking,,0,0,0,,With Gao Ding's surrender, Zhuge Liang regained the city of Yongchang.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.90,0:09:23.86,Thinking,,0,0,0,,There, he made preparations to battle against Meng Huo.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.34,0:10:35.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I have important news for the king.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.10,0:10:40.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Get out of the way!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.14,0:10:53.90,Default,,0,0,0,,King, my king!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.90,0:10:56.30,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\move(284.958,554.264,284.958,554.264,10,-30)}Mèng Huò
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.14,0:10:56.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Speak!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.94,0:10:59.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang has entered the city of Yongchang!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.02,0:11:00.66,Default,,0,0,0,,What!?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.34,0:11:04.14,Default,,0,0,0,,King!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.50,0:11:08.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that Zhuge Liang is approaching,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.06,0:11:09.86,Default,,0,0,0,,we will meet him in battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.14,0:11:13.82,Default,,0,0,0,,-Jinhuan Sanjie. \N-Here, my king.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.14,0:11:16.46,Default,,0,0,0,,-Dongtuna, Ahuinan!\N-Here, my king.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.46,0:11:19.66,Default,,0,0,0,,You three will attack the enemy along three routes, and be sure to succeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.90,0:11:21.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Aye!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.30,0:11:28.74,Default,,0,0,0,,As the saying goes, an onlooker sees farther than a participant.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.74,0:11:34.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Youchang, you are new here, what are your views on this expedition?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.38,0:11:35.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.26,0:11:37.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.02,0:11:39.70,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(319.792,497.208)}Mǎ Sù\NStyled: Yòucháng
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.14,0:11:41.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I have but one thought to share for your consideration.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.30,0:11:44.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Please do.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.30,0:11:49.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}Excuse my frankness, but for this expedition, capturing Meng Huo will be simple,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.82,0:11:52.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}{\pos(640,661.585)}but winning him over will be a challenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.38,0:11:53.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}{\pos(640,661.585)}Please explain.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.14,0:11:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.14,0:11:59.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}The Southern King, living in remote mountains, has never accepted us.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.86,0:12:04.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}We may defeat them now, \Nbut the troubles will continue after.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.14,0:12:11.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}If you defeat them now and proceed with the northern expedition,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.86,0:12:14.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}the Southern King will ravage our borders again for certain.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.90,0:12:18.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585\pos(640,678)}Then the troubles in the back line will not end.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.78,0:12:21.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585\pos(640,678)}In your view...?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.02,0:12:22.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585\pos(640,678)}In my view...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.50,0:12:26.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}To win the heart of the South is paramount; the conquest of cities a lesser concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.34,0:12:30.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}{\pos(640,661.585)}Win their favor over winning them with arms.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.74,0:12:35.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}Chancellor should gain the support of \Nthe Southerners to achieve peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.30,0:12:37.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}{\pos(640,661.585)}Then, we can march onwards to the North,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.82,0:12:40.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}{\pos(640,661.585)}to crown our great undertaking with success.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.14,0:12:46.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}"Winning hearts is paramount; the conquest of cities as a lesser concern..."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.46,0:12:51.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}{\pos(640,661.585)}It seems Youchang truly understands me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.62,0:12:57.98,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(330.51,558.34)}Āhuìnán
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.62,0:13:03.10,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(313.093,558.34)}Dǒngtúnà
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.90,0:13:25.74,Default,,0,0,0,,-My king! Grave news!\N-Speak!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.06,0:13:27.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Jinhuan Sanjie has fallen.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.74,0:13:29.34,Default,,0,0,0,,What of the other two marshals?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.46,0:13:32.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Dongtuna and Ahuinan have been captured!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.82,0:13:46.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Zhuge Liang, I swear to avenge this. \NI swear to avenge this!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.46,0:14:01.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Generals, I apologize for the fright.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.14,0:14:12.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.98,0:14:14.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, stand up.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.46,0:14:20.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Prepare a feast for quelling the generals' fright.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.78,0:14:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.38,0:14:24.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.22,0:14:29.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Gentlemen, my Emperor has always treated the South justly.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.66,0:14:32.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you serving by the king's side,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.14,0:14:35.02,Default,,0,0,0,,and bringing suffering to the people?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.46,0:14:43.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps this is a difficult matter for you two?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.22,0:14:52.46,Default,,0,0,0,,We, as vassals of Meng Huo,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.30,0:14:56.54,Default,,0,0,0,,had no other choice but to obey his orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.78,0:15:01.86,Default,,0,0,0,,For our offense towards the Chancellor, the guilt is on us.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.98,0:15:04.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Your words are mistaken, generals.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.90,0:15:08.14,Default,,0,0,0,,That we had to meet in battle was but a misunderstanding.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.38,0:15:11.54,Default,,0,0,0,,From now on, our enmity remains in the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.50,0:15:18.98,Default,,0,0,0,,The day when our realms can live in unity \Nwill be a boon to the nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.98,0:15:23.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, let us have a toast.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.90,0:15:26.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd like you to persuade King Meng Huo on your return,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.86,0:15:31.14,Default,,0,0,0,,to end this war, restore relations between our two sides, and benefit all our peoples.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.30,0:15:32.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I place my hope onto you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.14,0:15:37.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.94,0:15:38.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.14,0:15:46.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}{\pos(640,661.585)}These are silks of the land of Shu.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.46,0:15:50.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}I gift them to you as a mark of our everlasting friendship.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.22,0:15:55.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}The path from hostility to friendship is but a step away.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.14,0:15:57.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}{\pos(640,661.585)}I hope you can make that step forward.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.98,0:16:01.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor's kindness will be remembered.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.66,0:16:03.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.50,0:16:04.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Please stand.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.82,0:16:44.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Zilong, Wenchang, Zijun.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.10,0:16:45.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Present!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.38,0:16:48.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Though Meng Huo suffered a defeat today, he won't submit easily.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.62,0:16:53.10,Default,,0,0,0,,He is sure to come back himself to fight us with greater ferocity.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.54,0:16:54.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Zijun.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.34,0:16:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.30,0:16:59.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Lure him into an ambush and besiege him.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.70,0:17:00.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.38,0:17:03.22,Default,,0,0,0,,When Meng Huo is defeated, \Nhe will flee to the Jindai Mountain.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.22,0:17:04.94,Default,,0,0,0,,-Zilong, Wenchang. \N-Sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.14,0:17:07.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You two will go to the mountainside to lay an ambush.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.70,0:17:10.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Capture him alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.50,0:17:11.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.42,0:17:32.54,Default,,0,0,0,,A valiant King of the South.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.58,0:17:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,They say Zhuge Liang is \Nwell versed in the art of war.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.38,0:17:40.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet his formation is disorderly and in disarray. How can he win against me?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.46,0:17:44.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me teach him a lesson. Charge!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.06,0:17:59.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you running!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.94,0:18:29.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Meng Huo! Do you recognize Zhao Zilong of Changshan?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.82,0:19:13.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.42,0:19:19.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Move.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.98,0:19:31.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Move!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.50,0:20:02.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Move.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.26,0:20:10.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Kneel!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.14,0:20:27.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you Meng Huo?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.74,0:20:37.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that you are captured, will you submit?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.86,0:20:40.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I will not.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.90,0:20:58.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.50,0:21:03.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Give him back his weapons and his horse. \NSee him out of the camp.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.50,0:21:04.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, why-!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.02,0:21:07.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Speak no more. Go do as you are told.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.70,0:21:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.14,0:21:56.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, Meng Huo is the chieftain of the Southern Tribes.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.46,0:21:58.86,Default,,0,0,0,,We had just captured him, why do you set him free?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.90,0:22:02.34,Default,,0,0,0,,It is easy enough for me to capture him.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.78,0:22:05.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I could simply raise my hand to put him to death.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.02,0:22:07.94,Default,,0,0,0,,But to have Meng Huo accept us,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.94,0:22:11.22,Default,,0,0,0,,and to win the allegiance of the southern border, is no easy task.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.78,0:22:14.50,Default,,0,0,0,,That is the purpose of our expedition.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.74,0:22:30.02,Thinking,,0,0,0,,-The Chancellor is coming. \N-Many thanks, Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.14,0:22:31.46,Default,,0,0,0,,No need, no need.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.62,0:22:33.90,Default,,0,0,0,,You are all good people.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.34,0:22:36.82,Default,,0,0,0,,You were only forced by Meng Huo.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.26,0:22:41.82,Default,,0,0,0,,With your capture, no doubt your family and friends at home must be anxious,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.06,0:22:45.02,Default,,0,0,0,,expecting your safe return with worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.86,0:22:51.62,Default,,0,0,0,,I shall let you return home in order to alleviate their worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:52.58,0:22:56.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.78,0:22:59.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Please return home now.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.26,0:23:03.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, go.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.02,0:23:07.86,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.90,0:23:13.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.70,0:23:39.50,Default,,0,0,0,,The King has returned!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.26,0:23:47.10,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Open the gate!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.74,0:24:13.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I've broken past the enemy horde to return!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.78,0:24:19.02,Default,,0,0,0,,That Zhuge Liang's art of war is all mere trickery.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.18,0:24:22.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Our King's might can defeat all foes.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:24.98,0:24:27.22,Default,,0,0,0,,For now, we need to be on the defensive.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.78,0:24:34.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Another battle could lead us to another trick of his.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.86,0:24:38.46,Default,,0,0,0,,We have the Lu River as our natural barrier.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:38.54,0:24:41.46,Default,,0,0,0,,We will detain all boats on the river.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:42.14,0:24:47.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, build deep trenches and high fortresses along the bank and stand guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.46,0:24:52.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The men of Shu have journeyed long under our southern heat.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:52.66,0:24:56.70,Default,,0,0,0,,They are not accustomed to our lands and weather. \NHow could they stay for long?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.14,0:24:59.78,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(940.111,504)}Mèng Yōu
Dialogue: 0,0:24:59.78,0:25:03.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd like to see what other tricks Zhuge Liang has in his sleeve.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:04.14,0:25:06.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Second Brother, this plan will work.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:06.26,0:25:10.18,Default,,0,0,0,,The Lu River is just enough to resist Zhuge Liang's army.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.46,0:25:24.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, all the rafts have been detained by Meng Huo at the south bank.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.98,0:25:28.10,Default,,0,0,0,,They have also built defensive works along the river.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.62,0:25:33.26,Default,,0,0,0,,They are all well-guarded, and the currents are fast. It will be difficult to cross.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:40.06,0:25:45.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Pass my order: we have made our arrival, so we won't return empty handed.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:46.82,0:25:53.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Under this heat, have the camps set up near the mountains at spots with lush vegetation.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.18,0:26:00.58,Default,,0,0,0,,After Ma Dai arrives with the provisions and medicine, we will begin the attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:01.78,0:26:02.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:30.54,0:26:33.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Meng Huo is defending the Lu River and has detained all the boats.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.30,0:26:37.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Our soldiers are tired after all the fighting.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.78,0:26:42.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Are the three thousand troops you have brought ready to advance?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.54,0:26:44.54,Style Names,,0,0,0,,{\pos(987.004,464.604)}Mǎ Dài
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.62,0:26:44.54,Default,,0,0,0,,They are at your service.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:46.78,0:26:50.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, I plan to cut off his supply line first,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.98,0:26:52.26,Default,,0,0,0,,and let them fall to disarray.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:52.38,0:26:54.46,Default,,0,0,0,,How shall this be done?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:54.78,0:27:01.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Liushakou is 150{\i1} li{\i0} away from here, in the lower reaches of this river.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.42,0:27:05.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The waters there are shallow and calm, \Nso you can make rafts and cross.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:05.86,0:27:08.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You will lead your three thousand troops to sneak across,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:08.98,0:27:10.34,Default,,0,0,0,,and advance into his ravine.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:10.62,0:27:12.26,Default,,0,0,0,, Then, cut off his provision supplies.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:12.82,0:27:15.42,Default,,0,0,0,,His soldiers will fall into chaos.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:16.02,0:27:21.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Afterwards, you will coordinate with Chieftains Dongtuna and Ahuinan, who will act from within.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.50,0:27:23.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Meng Huo will be captured.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:23.50,0:27:24.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Aye, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.34,0:27:59.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Heaven bless me and let the soldiers of Zhuge Liang be poisoned in the River of Lu.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:16.14,0:28:18.02,Default,,0,0,0,,General, the waters are shallow!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.02,0:28:19.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Any sight of soldiers at the opposite bank?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:20.06,0:28:21.30,Default,,0,0,0,,No soldiers, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:26.66,0:28:29.82,Default,,0,0,0,,-Orders: cross the river! \N{\i1}-Cross the river!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:51.98,0:28:55.22,Thinking,,0,0,0,,I'm covered in stink! Perfect timing to take a bath!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.14,0:28:58.26,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Hey, the water's so warm!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.38,0:29:13.38,Thinking,,0,0,0,,What a blast!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:21.58,0:29:22.74,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Why am I feeling tipsy?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:26.54,0:29:27.78,Thinking,,0,0,0,,I can't do it anymore!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:32.22,0:29:33.70,Thinking,,0,0,0,,There's poison in this water!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:35.30,0:29:36.62,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Help me!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:48.90,0:29:50.10,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Help me!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:59.30,0:30:00.30,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Get on the shore!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:05.74,0:30:10.02,Default,,0,0,0,,General, the water is poisoned!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.90,0:30:15.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Retreat! Retreat!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:16.26,0:30:19.18,Thinking,,0,0,0,,Come up! Get on the shore now!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:09.58,0:31:11.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:31:14.58,0:31:19.02,Default,,0,0,0,,The Shu men all fainted when they got into the water of Shakou.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:21.10,0:31:23.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Was Zhuge Liang there?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:23.90,0:31:25.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Haven't seen him, general.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:28.02,0:31:29.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Then who was the commander?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:29.78,0:31:33.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I saw banners with the name Ma Dai, General of Pacifying the North.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:34.66,0:31:35.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Ma Dai?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:37.10,0:31:38.78,Default,,0,0,0,,-You may go.\N-Aye.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.30,0:31:43.62,Default,,0,0,0,,-Elder Brother. \N-Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:44.82,0:31:48.98,Default,,0,0,0,,You stay here, I will go meet with the Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:48.98,0:31:53.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright. I'll take care of things here, don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:16.38,0:32:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:17.54,0:32:19.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Please rise. Please rise.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:21.46,0:32:25.66,Default,,0,0,0,,General, you have arrived so late at night. \NYou must have something important to share?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:26.86,0:32:30.74,Default,,0,0,0,,With all the boats detained by Meng Huo, and the south bank occupied,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:30.74,0:32:35.02,Default,,0,0,0,,now he's using the river's poison to stop your righteous army.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:36.02,0:32:39.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, General Ma Dai has become a victim of these tactics.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:42.30,0:32:45.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you have a way out to cross the river, general?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:47.18,0:32:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}{\pos(640,661.585)}There is miasma in the Lu River.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:49.34,0:32:52.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}When the heat of the sun evaporates the river water, it turns into poison gas.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:53.14,0:32:56.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}Attempting to cross the river during the day will lead to certain death!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:01.42,0:33:05.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}For Chancellor to cross the river, you must wait until nightfall when the water cools.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:05.90,0:33:11.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}The poison will not rise, and any healthy and fed man can cross safely.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:12.26,0:33:16.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}{\pos(640,661.585)}I myself crossed the river at this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:18.98,0:33:21.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}{\pos(640,661.585)}Thank you very much for your kind guidance.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:24.26,0:33:30.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}I cannot ever repay enough of the Chancellor's kindness.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:31.94,0:33:35.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}But now I must hurry back\N so that I will not be discovered,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.90,0:33:39.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\bord13.585}{\pos(640,661.585)}and let Marshal Dongtuna be burdened.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.82,0:33:44.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Then please do hurry back, General. Take care of yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:48.02,0:33:49.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:52.34,0:33:55.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Farewell, generals.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.58,0:34:24.74,Default,,0,0,0,,We can cross now.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:25.78,0:34:29.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Night has fallen and the water is cool; \Nshall we start the crossing?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.58,0:34:39.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Cross the river.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:26.74,0:35:28.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Great king!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:30.50,0:35:34.42,Default,,0,0,0,,My king, the Shu army has crossed the river!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:35.30,0:35:38.66,Default,,0,0,0,,They've cut off the supply line at Jiashan Valley!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:40.78,0:35:41.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it true?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:41.66,0:35:44.42,Default,,0,0,0,,My king, absolutely!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:45.90,0:35:51.54,Default,,0,0,0,,My king, General Mangyazhang went to fight them...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:53.62,0:35:55.94,Default,,0,0,0,,...but he was slain in battle by a Shu general!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:02.18,0:36:03.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is this Shu general?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:06.06,0:36:08.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Ma Dai, General of Pacifying the North.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:08.90,0:36:09.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Ma Dai?
Dialogue: 0,0:36:15.02,0:36:15.90,Default,,0,0,0,,My king.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:15.90,0:36:21.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Marshal Dongtuna, I order you to defeat Ma Dai immediately and restore our supply line.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:24.86,0:36:25.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Aye.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:07.22,0:37:10.74,Default,,0,0,0,,General, this man has been released by the Chancellor before.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:11.70,0:37:14.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh yeah, that's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:22.42,0:37:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you Marshal Dongtuna?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:28.46,0:37:29.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:46.14,0:37:46.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Go.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:54.66,0:37:55.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Dongtuna.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:56.66,0:37:59.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Is the supply line at Jiashan Valley restored?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:01.06,0:38:04.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Ma Dai is a great warrior, I am not his equal.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:04.90,0:38:06.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Humph, liar!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:07.54,0:38:10.58,Default,,0,0,0,,It's obvious you feel indebted to Zhuge Liang,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:10.66,0:38:14.50,Default,,0,0,0,,so you retreated without a fight, \Nand now you try to fool me.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:15.22,0:38:16.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Take him away. Kill him!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:16.82,0:38:17.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:19.98,0:38:24.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Great king, General Dong is guilty of not fighting the enemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:24.02,0:38:26.62,Default,,0,0,0,,but I beg you to spare his life for the sake of his past services.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:26.62,0:38:31.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Please give him the chance to make amends.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:33.42,0:38:34.58,Default,,0,0,0,,My king!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:36.42,0:38:38.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder Brother, the enemy is pressing on to the border.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:38.62,0:38:40.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Killing a general now is not suitable.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:42.10,0:38:43.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's give him a chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:47.26,0:38:48.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Elder Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:50.98,0:38:55.26,Default,,0,0,0,,On account of his friendship over the years, I'll spare his life.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:55.50,0:38:59.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, be grateful to the king for his mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:02.50,0:39:05.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Get him out. One hundred lashes as punishment.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:05.02,0:39:05.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Aye!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:07.26,0:39:08.26,Default,,0,0,0,,My king!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:31.18,0:39:34.22,Default,,0,0,0,,The king is determined to fight against the Shu forces.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:34.38,0:39:39.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Sooner or later, we'll either die on the battlefield, or be killed by him.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:43.02,0:39:46.02,Default,,0,0,0,,The tribal chiefs under my command all say,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:46.30,0:39:49.26,Default,,0,0,0,,many were forced by Meng Huo to rebel.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:51.06,0:39:54.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Many are indebted to Chancellor \NZhuge Liang for saving their lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:54.78,0:39:57.30,Default,,0,0,0,,None of them want to continue this war anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:58.06,0:40:00.94,Default,,0,0,0,,That Chancellor Zhuge Liang has a divine wit and foresight,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:01.10,0:40:03.70,Default,,0,0,0,,even Cao Cao and Sun Quan were wary of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:04.18,0:40:06.38,Default,,0,0,0,,How can our king ever win?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:06.98,0:40:13.66,Default,,0,0,0,,The Chancellor has treated us with great kindness, how can we still fight against them?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:16.46,0:40:20.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Both of us owe our lives to the Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:20.46,0:40:24.18,Default,,0,0,0,,We all feel uneasy about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:24.18,0:40:27.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, we should kill Meng Huo ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:34.78,0:40:38.54,Default,,0,0,0,,We kill Meng Huo and submit to the Chancellor,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:38.74,0:40:43.26,Default,,0,0,0,,then we can prevent further suffering of the ravine's soldiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:52.54,0:40:56.82,Default,,0,0,0,,No, we must capture him alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:59.86,0:41:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, we hand him over to the Chancellor.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:24.58,0:41:25.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Halt, generals.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:48.54,0:41:53.86,Default,,0,0,0,,You said before that you would surrender if you were captured again.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:53.86,0:41:55.82,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you have to say now?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:56.38,0:41:59.22,Default,,0,0,0,,This was not your doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:00.10,0:42:03.18,Default,,0,0,0,,This was the result of my own men's infighting.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:03.50,0:42:06.70,Default,,0,0,0,,With that in mind, how could I submit?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:12.98,0:42:15.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright, how about I set you free once again?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:16.86,0:42:19.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Though I am a Southerner, I also know the art of war.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:19.50,0:42:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,If you let me back to my ravine this time,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:21.38,0:42:22.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I will come back with my army to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:22.98,0:42:26.70,Default,,0,0,0,,If you manage to capture me then, I'll submit myself to you wholeheartedly.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:26.90,0:42:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,This I promise.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:28.42,0:42:30.78,Default,,0,0,0,,If you are captured again, but refuse to submit,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:32.18,0:42:33.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I will not show mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:44.62,0:42:48.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Our army is elite and well supplied, with great and capable warrior-generals.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:48.82,0:42:53.22,Default,,0,0,0,,With their morale and spirits high, how do you plan to win?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:54.98,0:42:56.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Should you surrender early,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:56.98,0:43:01.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I can present a memorial to the Emperor so that you will keep your status as king,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:01.54,0:43:05.10,Default,,0,0,0,,and all your descendants will remain as the leaders of your people.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:06.50,0:43:09.22,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you think of that?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:11.30,0:43:15.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I myself could yield, but I fear my subjects would not obey.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:15.46,0:43:17.54,Default,,0,0,0,,If Chancellor can let me go,
Dialogue: 0,0:43:17.54,0:43:20.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I will call them over to pledge our allegiance to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:30.18,0:43:30.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.

